---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ApiCard from '../components/ApiCard.astro';
import {apis,reviewed,categories,categorySlug} from '../lib/catalog';
import {guides} from '../lib/guides';
const picks=['radio-browser','open-meteo','frankfurter','jsonplaceholder','open-library','pokeapi'].map(id=>apis.find(a=>a.slug===id));
const topics=[['Weather','☀','Forecast your next project.'],['Music & audio','♫','Tune into something new.'],['Finance','↗','Put numbers in context.'],['Science','⌬','Explore a world of data.'],['Development','⌘','Prototype at full speed.'],['Books & culture','▤','Find stories worth building.']];
const faqs=[['What is Endpoint?','Endpoint is an independent directory of public APIs. It combines attributed community catalogs with individually researched guides and a client-side request playground.'],['Are all listed APIs free?','No. Some offer free access or a limited free tier; others require payment. “No key” describes authentication, not pricing or commercial-use permission. Imported listings say “Check pricing” until reviewed.'],['Can I try an API without leaving the site?','Yes, when the provider permits browser requests through CORS. Use an example from a reviewed guide or enter your own endpoint in the playground. Credentials stay in page memory and are sent directly to the selected provider.'],['What does “Docs reviewed” mean?','The guide was checked against provider documentation on the stated date. It is not a guarantee of availability, a live uptime test, or an endorsement. Community listings have not been individually verified.']];
---
<Base title="Discover public APIs. Build your next idea." description="Explore 2,112 public APIs in 50 categories. Compare access requirements, read 32 reviewed guides, and try requests in a browser-only API playground."><main id="main"><section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> A DIRECTORY FOR PEOPLE WHO BUILD</div><h1>Great ideas<br/>start with<br/><em>the right API.</em></h1><p>Find your building blocks. Understand the fine print.<br class="desktop"/> Make your first request, all in one place.</p><form class="hero-search" action="/library/" role="search"><label class="sr-only" for="hero-query">Search the API library</label><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><input id="hero-query" name="q" placeholder="Weather, radio, books…" type="search"/><button class="button" type="submit">Explore APIs <span>↗</span></button></form><div class="popular"><span>Start with</span><a href="/categories/music-audio/">Radio & music</a><a href="/categories/weather/">Weather</a><a href="/collections/no-api-key/">No API key</a></div></div><div class="hero-visual"><div class="floating-label">FROM AN IDEA TO YOUR FIRST RESPONSE <span>↘</span></div><div class="demo-window"><div class="window-bar"><span class="window-dots">● ● ●</span><span>your-next-project.js</span><span>↗</span></div><div class="demo-request"><span class="method">GET</span><span>api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast</span></div><div class="demo-code"><code><span class="code-muted">// A little data. A lot of possibilities.</span><br/><span class="code-purple">const</span> response = <span class="code-purple">await</span> fetch(url);<br/><span class="code-purple">const</span> weather = <span class="code-purple">await</span> response.json();</code></div><div class="demo-response"><div><span class="success-dot"></span> Example response <span class="code-muted">illustrative data</span></div><pre><span class="code-muted">{`{`}</span>
  <span class="code-lime">"latitude"</span>: <span class="code-orange">42.7</span>,
  <span class="code-lime">"longitude"</span>: <span class="code-orange">23.32</span>,
  <span class="code-lime">"current"</span>: {`{`}
    <span class="code-lime">"temperature_2m"</span>: <span class="code-orange">21.4</span>
  {`}`}
<span class="code-muted">{`}`}</span></pre></div><a class="demo-link" href="/apis/open-meteo/#playground">Make a real request <span>→</span></a></div><div class="visual-caption"><span class="caption-icon">↗</span><span>From “what if?”<br/><strong>to “it works.”</strong></span></div></div></section><section class="stats-strip"><div class="wrap stats"><div><strong>{apis.length.toLocaleString('en-US')}</strong><span>APIs to discover</span></div><div><strong>{categories.length}</strong><span>categories to explore</span></div><div><strong>{reviewed.length}</strong><span>documentation-reviewed guides</span></div><div><strong>100%</strong><span>client-side request playground</span></div></div></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">A GOOD PLACE TO START</div><h2>Small requests.<br/><em>Big possibilities.</em></h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/collections/docs-reviewed/">All reviewed guides <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="api-grid featured-grid">{picks.map(a=><ApiCard api={a}/>)}</div></section><section class="category-section"><div class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">FOLLOW YOUR CURIOSITY</div><h2>What are you building?</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/library/">Browse all 50 categories ↗</a></div><div class="topic-grid">{topics.map(([name,icon,desc])=><a class="topic-card" href={`/categories/${categorySlug(name)}/`}><span class="topic-icon">{icon}</span><h3>{name}</h3><p>{desc}</p><span class="topic-count">{categories.find(c=>c.name===name)?.count} APIs <span>↗</span></span></a>)}</div></div></section><section class="wrap section workflow"><div><div class="eyebrow">LESS GUESSWORK. MORE BUILDING.</div><h2>Discovery is just<br/><em>the beginning.</em></h2><p class="section-intro">An API name isn’t enough. Get the context you need to choose it—and the tools to understand what comes back.</p><a class="button" href="/playground/">Open the playground <span>↗</span></a></div><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Find the right fit</h3><p>Search by topic, filter by access, and start with documentation-reviewed guides.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Read between the limits</h3><p>Understand authentication, usage conditions, and the difference between a free endpoint and a free production plan.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>See what you’re working with</h3><p>Edit a request, add your own test credentials, and explore JSON as a tree or table. Copy a request when you’re ready.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="wrap section guides-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU SHIP</div><h2>A little context goes a long way.</h2></div></div><div class="guide-grid">{guides.map((g,i)=><a class="guide-card" href={`/guides/${g.slug}/`}><span class="guide-number">0{i+1} / {g.label}</span><h3>{g.title}</h3><p>{g.description}</p><span class="text-link">Read the guide ↗</span></a>)}</div></section><section class="wrap section faq-section"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE FINE PRINT, MADE CLEAR</div><h2>Good questions.</h2><p>Independent, source-aware, and built for a practical first look.</p></div><div class="faq-list">{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}<span>+</span></summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</div></section><section class="wrap final-cta"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT PROJECT IS CALLING</div><h2>Find its first building block.</h2></div><a class="button light" href="/library/">Explore the library <span>↗</span></a></section></main></Base>
